  {
    "episode_id": 84195,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84195.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "And that's no surprise. And now, of course, you've been doing some other work as well, even though this resolution is your first bill. You've been hard at work. You've been chairing the subcommittee on elections in the US House of Representatives. And today, as we speak Friday, the 10th, you held a hearing on the 2022 midterms and kind of a post-mortem kind of a look back. Of course, it's no secret. You have a lot of experience with elections as the former secretary of state of Florida. And what member what message rather should voters take away from what you found at the hearing today?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
