  {
    "episode_id": 84195,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84195.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Now, one of the things you mentioned in your opening statements at this hearing is the importance of sharing information among states. And in the news this past week, three states, including Florida, have pulled out of Eric, which is a system that, and you are surely more familiar with it than I, of checking voter rolls and sharing voter information between states to, among other things, I'm sure, make sure nobody votes twice. And I'm not going to ask you to second-guess Florida's decision, but I will ask about the role that Congress can play in encouraging states to keep sharing that kind of information, and if there's a congressional response to the situation with Eric.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The speaker acknowledges that sharing information among states is important.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Three states, including Florida, have withdrawn from the ERIC system.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "ERIC is a system used for checking voter rolls and sharing voter information between states.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "One purpose of ERIC is to help prevent individuals from voting more than once.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker does not expect the listener to critique Florida’s decision to leave ERIC.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Congress has the potential to encourage states to continue participating in information-sharing systems like ERIC.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Maintaining accurate voter rolls through inter-state data sharing is a valuable public good.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "State decisions to withdraw from shared systems may undermine national election integrity.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Congress possesses legitimate authority to influence state-level participation in federal-aligned initiatives.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "There is value in preserving mechanisms that detect double voting.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience is expected to understand the technical function of ERIC without further explanation.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
