    "turn_text": "Well, we are so fortunate to have a talented and experienced Florida delegation up here representing our state. The other members have been so welcoming to me And really the most important thing that we do is come up here to represent the people who elected us. And that means the values and the priorities of our community. And in some cases, it's an opportunity for us to really shine a light on some of the things that make our community special. And that's why I was so pleased to support my first bill since taking office, which related to plant city strawberry festival, because that is such a unique and special thing about Florida's 15th congressional district. We are the winter strawberry capital of the world implant city producing 75% of the nation's midwinter crop. And that's one of the things that makes Florida's 15th district special. So for me, serving up here in Washington, D.C., I have the opportunity to work on some really important policy issues. cybersecurity, elections, the many things that we'll be coming through to the Judiciary Committee. But I also get the privilege of getting to tell the story of our 15th district and all of the things that make it special.",
